{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791134378,"nonce":"mWxFFPnd/dOyGiDMyYbDO3orA+A=","title":"hxx: ref bindings, so an element in a template can be named without breaking the template up","message":"hxx has no `ref`: `\u003cdiv ref={panel}\u003e` is an error (\"\u003cdiv\u003e has no attribute ref\"). To bind behaviour to an element inside a template, you split the template into `var` declarations and nest them back with `{panel}`. tools/demo/LiquidGlass.hx had to build its card as three templates for that reason, `close`, then `panel` holding `{close}`, then the root holding `{panel}`, just to reach two nodes.\n\nWanted: a typed `Ref\u003cT:Element\u003e` that a template fills as it builds:\n\n    var panel = new Ref\u003cDiv\u003e(), close = new Ref\u003cDiv\u003e();\n    var root = hxx('\n        \u003cdiv padding={20}\u003e\n            \u003cdiv ref={panel} class=\"rounded-3xl\" ...\u003e\n                \u003cdiv ref={close} class=\"rounded-full\"\u003e...\u003c/div\u003e\n            \u003c/div\u003e\n        \u003c/div\u003e\n    ');\n    query(panel).onPointerDown(e -\u003e drag(e));\n    query(close).onClick(_ -\u003e quit());\n\n- `ref` is accepted on every built-in tag and on components. Its type is checked against the tag's element type, so `ref={panel}` on a `\u003cdiv\u003e` wants a `Ref\u003cDiv\u003e`, and on a component a `Ref` of that component's class.\n- A Ref is set when the element is built and cleared when its owner disposes it, so a ref inside `\u003cif\u003e` or `\u003cfor\u003e` follows the element that is there now.\n- Reading a Ref is tracked, as a signal is, so a computed or watch that reads it runs again when it is set. `query(ref)` binds as soon as the ref has an element, and binds again to the new one when it changes.\n- Inside `\u003cfor\u003e`, a `Ref` per item, or a `RefList\u003cT\u003e` collecting them; decide which.\n\n`query` (git-bug 8ec2dd9) takes a Ref as well as an element.","files":null}]}